    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d505">

                <pb facs="0785" n="767" sameAs="frus:frus1946v05/pg767"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.6362/2–1146: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the United States Political
                        Adviser for Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Murphy</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-11T20:00:00-05:00">February 11, 1946—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>387. French Govt has presented to Dept <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >aide-mémoire</hi><anchor n="57" xml:id="d505-f1"/> protesting statement
                    allegedly made by US representative Economic Directorate in meeting of Jan 10.
                    US position described as having been that since German domestic coal
                    requirements were not being met that no expansion in coal exports could be
                    considered. French position described as having been that coal exports should be
                    maximized within limits of transport capabilities. French protest made on basis
                    alleged US position violates July coal directive.<anchor n="58" xml:id="d505-f2"
                    /></p>
                <p>Would you report fully relevant portion Jan 10 meeting.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d505-f1" n="57" xml:id="d505-f1-content">
                <p>Dated February 8, not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d505-f2" n="58" xml:id="d505-f2-content">
                <p>For text of the directive issued to General Eisenhower by the Joint Chiefs of
                    Staff, July 26, 1945, see <ref target="frus1945Berlinv02#pg_1028"><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, The Conference of Berlin
                        (The Potsdam Conference), 1945, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, p.
                        1028</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
